---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import PdfResources from '@/components/PdfResources.astro';
import '@/styles/german-lesson-five.css';
const nouns = [
 ['das Bett','bed'],['das Bild','picture'],['der Boden','floor'],['die Farbe','colour'],
 ['die Flasche','bottle'],['das Geld','money'],['das Handy','mobile phone'],['das Haus','house'],
 ['der Laptop','laptop'],['der Ausweis','ID card'],['das Regal','shelf'],['der Rucksack','backpack'],
 ['der Schreibtisch','desk'],['der Schlüssel','key'],['die Schule','school'],['das Studentenwohnheim','student residence'],
 ['der Stuhl','chair'],['die Tasche','bag'],['die Tasse','cup'],['der Teppich','carpet'],
 ['das Telefon','telephone'],['die Universität','university'],['die Wand','wall'],['das Wasser','water'],['das Zimmer','room']
];
---
<Base title="German Lesson 7 extension: Colours and possessives" description="Extended writing, possessive-adjective practice, and nouns for Lesson 7 of Grenzenlos Deutsch.">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/german/lesson-seven.css" />
  <div class="lesson-five lesson-seven">
    <header class="lesson-hero"><div class="wrap"><a class="back" href="/resources/german-lesson-7">← Back to Lesson 7</a><p class="eyebrow">UNIT 01 · LESSON 07 · ERWEITERUNG</p><h1 lang="de">Farben <em>weiter üben.</em></h1><p class="intro">Extend your colour vocabulary, write about a room, and practise possessive adjectives with feedback.</p><p class="context">Follows the original <a href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/e1/l7/erw/">Grenzenlos Deutsch Lesson 7 extension</a>: Schreiben → Strukturen → Wortschatz.</p><nav class="step-nav" aria-label="Extension sections"><a href="#writing">01 Writing</a><a href="#structures">02 Grammar</a><a href="#vocabulary">03 Vocabulary</a><a href="#study-resources">04 PDF</a></nav></div></header>
    <div class="wrap lesson-body">
      <section id="writing" aria-labelledby="writing-title"><p class="eyebrow">01 / SCHREIBEN</p><h2 id="writing-title">Describe a room.</h2><figure class="lesson-activity-image"><img src="/assets/german/lesson7-images/paper_activity_sm.jpg" alt="Pencil and paper from the original writing activity" loading="lazy" width="150" height="150"/><figcaption>Original writing-activity illustration.</figcaption></figure><p>Write at least ten complete sentences naming things in your room and describing their colours. Use vocabulary such as <em lang="de">der Stuhl, das Bett, der Schreibtisch, der Teppich, der Boden, die Wand, das Handy, das Buch, das Regal, die Tasche</em>.</p><div class="dialogue"><p lang="de">Mein Stuhl ist grau.</p><p lang="de">Meine Tasche ist schwarz.</p><p lang="de">Mein Bett ist weiß, und mein Teppich ist blau.</p></div><label class="write-label" for="room-writing">Your German description (saved only while this page is open)</label><textarea id="room-writing" rows="9" placeholder="Mein Zimmer ist ..."></textarea><p class="small">This is a private writing area. It is not submitted to a server; copy your answer before leaving the page.</p></section>
      <section id="structures" aria-labelledby="structures-title"><p class="eyebrow">02 / STRUKTUREN</p><h2 id="structures-title">Choose the right possessive form.</h2><p>As you saw in the main lesson, the base forms are <em lang="de">mein, dein, sein, ihr, unser, euer</em> and formal <em lang="de">Ihr</em>. They change depending on noun and case. Here the nouns are subjects, so notice <em lang="de">mein Buch</em> (neuter) but <em lang="de">meine Tasche</em> (feminine).</p><div class="grammar-grid"><article><h3>Singular possessives</h3><ul><li lang="de">ich → mein / meine</li><li lang="de">du → dein / deine</li><li lang="de">er → sein / seine</li><li lang="de">sie → ihr / ihre</li></ul></article><article><h3>Plural or formal</h3><ul><li lang="de">wir → unser / unsere</li><li lang="de">ihr → euer / eure</li><li lang="de">sie (they) → ihr / ihre</li><li lang="de">Sie (formal) → Ihr / Ihre</li></ul></article></div><div class="tip"><strong>From the source lesson:</strong> <span lang="de">Woher kommst du? Meine Familie kommt aus Hamburg.</span> The extension also discusses nonbinary language alternatives; these forms are evolving and vary across speakers.</div><h3 class="subheading">Practice with feedback</h3><form class="auto-quiz quiz-form"><fieldset data-answer="Meine"><legend>01 · ___ Familie kommt aus Hamburg. (my)</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="e1" value="Mein"/> Mein</label><label><input type="radio" name="e1" value="Meine"/> Meine</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset><fieldset data-answer="dein"><legend>02 · Wie heißt ___ Bruder? (your, informal)</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="e2" value="dein"/> dein</label><label><input type="radio" name="e2" value="deine"/> deine</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset><fieldset data-answer="Ihr"><legend>03 · Ist es ___ Buch? (your, formal)</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="e3" value="Ihr"/> Ihr</label><label><input type="radio" name="e3" value="Ihre"/> Ihre</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset><fieldset data-answer="Unser"><legend>04 · ___ Haus ist klein. (our)</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="e4" value="Unser"/> Unser</label><label><input type="radio" name="e4" value="Unsere"/> Unsere</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset><div class="quiz-actions"><button type="submit">Check answers</button><button class="secondary" type="reset">Try again</button></div><p class="quiz-score" role="status"></p></form></section>
      <section id="vocabulary" aria-labelledby="vocabulary-title"><p class="eyebrow">03 / WORTSCHATZ</p><h2 id="vocabulary-title">Objects and colours to review.</h2><p>Learn these nouns with their articles. German nouns are capitalised. For plural details, consult the <a href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/e1/l7/erw/">original extension vocabulary list</a>.</p><div class="nouns-grid">{nouns.map(([de,en]) => <div><strong lang="de">{de}</strong><span>{en}</span></div>)}</div><p class="tip"><strong>Colours:</strong> <span lang="de">blau, braun, gelb, grau, grün, lila, orange, rosa, rot, schwarz, weiß</span>.</p><a class="next" href="/resources/german-lesson-8">Continue to Lesson 8 →</a></section>
      <div id="study-resources"><PdfResources lessonNumbers={[7]} /></div><aside class="source"><h2>Source and licence</h2><p>Adapted from the user-provided <a href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/e1/l7/erw/">Grenzenlos Deutsch: Lektion 7, Erweiterung</a> under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. The original writing-activity image is retained; practice questions are newly authored alternatives to unavailable H5P materials.</p></aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<script is:inline src="/assets/german/lesson-seven-interactions.js"></script>
